            <ArticleTitle>Polycyclic aromatic azomethine ylides: a unique entry to extended polycyclic heteroaromatics.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>436-441</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1039/c4sc02793k</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Based on polycyclic aromatic azomethine ylides (PAMYs), a metal-free &quot;cycloaddition-planarization-sequence&quot; is proposed, providing a unique entry to extended nitrogen-containing polycyclic aromatic hydrocarbons (N-PAHs). This method is highly versatile, as the structure of unprecedented N-PAHs can be tailored by the dipolarophile in the crucial 1,3-cycloaddition-reaction. Linear, as well as five- and six-membered cyclic dipolarophiles are successfully used. The geometric and optoelectronic nature of N-PAHs are investigated by UV-vis absorption and single crystal structure analysis. Remarkably, the newly synthesized N-PAHs demonstrate varying absorption profiles, covering the whole visible light range with rich photophysical properties, for example, fluorescent quantum yields up to 54%.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
